  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0184 database is a comprehensive schema that contains nine tables, each representing a distinct entity or relationship in the system. The User table contains information about the users of the system, including their phone number, password, email, first name, middle name, last name, date of birth, and address. The Food table contains information about the food items available for purchase, including their name, price, availability, rating, quantity, and description. The Restaurant table contains information about the restaurants that sell the food items, including their name, founding date, address, rating, and description. The CustomerService table contains information about the customer service inquiries, including the email address of the customer, the name of the customer, the inquiry, the status, and the submission date. The OrderHistory table contains information about the orders placed by the users, including the order ID, the user ID, the total price, the order date, and the foreign key referencing the User table. The Products table contains information about the products purchased by the users, including the product ID, the user ID, the order ID, the product, and the foreign keys referencing the User and OrderHistory tables. The Interacts table contains information about the interactions between the users and the customer service, including the interaction ID, the customer service ID, the user ID, and the foreign keys referencing the CustomerService and User tables. The Buys table contains information about the food items purchased by the users, including the buy ID, the user ID, the food ID, and the foreign keys referencing the User and Food tables. The Sells table contains information about the food items sold by the restaurants, including the sell ID, the restaurant ID, the food ID, and the foreign keys referencing the Restaurant and Food tables.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nTunisia faces a significant issue with food waste, with average food waste per family amounting to 5% of total food expenditure. The UN Food and Agriculture Organization reports high annual rates of food waste globally, impacting resources and economies. In Tunisia, this waste contributes to local shortages and hinders access to affordable food for low-income populations.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe objective is to develop a MySQL-based implementation of EcoEats, a MERN stack web application designed to manage food waste. The platform will enable businesses such as hotels, bakeries, restaurants, and supermarkets to sell excess food items at reduced prices, aiming to minimize food waste and provide affordable food options.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders: Business owners (hotels, restaurants, bakeries, supermarkets), platform administrators, government agencies focused on food waste reduction.\n- Users: Low-income individuals, general customers looking for affordable food options, customer service representatives.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. User Management:\n   - Registration and authentication of users with personal details, including contact information and addresses.\n   - Users can update personal information and view past order history.\n\n2. Product Management:\n   - Businesses can list excess food items with details such as name, price, availability, and description.\n   - Products can be associated with specific restaurants or sellers.\n\n3. Ordering System:\n   - Users can browse the available food items, place orders, and make secure payments.\n   - System to track order histories and manage purchases.\n\n4. Customer Service:\n   - Provide a platform for user inquiries, managed by customer service representatives.\n   - Track status and respond to customer service inquiries.\n\n5. Interactions with Businesses:\n   - Facilitate interaction between users and the businesses selling food items.\n   - Manage records of products sold by businesses.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: The system should support seamless interactions and manage a significant number of concurrent users.\n- Scalability: The platform should be able to scale with an increase in the number of users and transactions.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of user data and payment transactions.\n- Usability: The platform should be user-friendly, accessible, and intuitive for both sellers and buyers.\n- Reliability: The application should consistently function as intended with minimal downtime.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0184.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0184\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `food` (\n  `food_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `availability` boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,\n  `rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`food_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant` (\n  `restaurant_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `founding_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`restaurant_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer_service` (\n  `customer_service_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `inquiry` text NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `submission_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_service_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_history` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_history_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `products` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `products_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `products_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order_history` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `interacts` (\n  `interaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`interaction_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `interacts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_service_id`) REFERENCES `customer_service` (`customer_service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `interacts_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `buys` (\n  `buy_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `food_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`buy_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `buys_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `buys_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`food_id`) REFERENCES `food` (`food_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sells` (\n  `sell_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `restaurant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `food_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sell_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sells_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`restaurant_id`) REFERENCES `restaurant` (`restaurant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sells_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`food_id`) REFERENCES `food` (`food_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
